Lin et al., Nat. Commun. 15, 550 (2024), SM Sec. 3G: eight bands from four
spinful orbitals, and the no-go criterion on two gaps of the one Hamiltonian.
Bands are counted from 0, as pythtb counts them.

1. the model, its two Wyckoff orbits and all eight bands
   realized group   : #99.164 P4mm1', orbitals at Wyckoff 1a and 2c, 8 bands
   the 1a orbit     : -GM6 + -GM7 + -M6 + -M7 + 2x-X5
   the 2c orbit     : -GM6 + -GM7 + -M6 + -M7 + 2x-X5
   all 8 bands      : 2x-GM6 + 2x-GM7 + 2x-M6 + 2x-M7 + 4x-X5
   atomic limits    : 6 sums of elementary band representations, at
                      1a+1a+1a+1a, 1a+1a+1b+1b, 1a+1a+2c, 1b+1b+1b+1b, 1b+1b+2c, 2c+2c
   the model's own  : 1a+1a+2c, -E1 at 1a (4mm1') + -E2 at 1a (4mm1')
                      + -E at 2c (mm21')
   srsi_of_model(r) : the invariants of the model and of each Wyckoff orbit
   P4mm1' #99.164, double-valued: stable real-space invariants   (.group)
     the whole model: theta_1 to theta_3 = (2, 2, 0); theta_4, theta_5 = (0, 1) mod 2   (.theta_Z, .theta_Zn)
     each Wyckoff orbit, its site irreps written m (irrep)_w, with theta_1 to theta_3 and theta_4, theta_5 mod 2   (.wyckoff_orbits)
       1a (4mm1'): orbital 0, 1 (-E1)_a: (0, 1, 0); (0, 0) mod 2
       1a (4mm1'): orbital 1, 1 (-E2)_a: (1, 0, 0); (0, 0) mod 2
       2c (mm21'): orbitals 2-3, 1 (-E)_c: (1, 1, 0); (0, 1) mod 2
   the two orbits have one content and different Z2-valued invariants; the eight
   bands are three elementary band representations at two Wyckoff positions, an
   atomic insulator, not the one whose splittings the supplement tabulates

2. bands 4 and 5: the Z2-valued invariants come from the orbitals, not the bands
   bands 4 and 5    : -GM6 + -M7 + -X5
   atomic limit     : -E2 at 1b (4mm1')
   srsi_of_bands    : Z-valued (0, 0, 1), and no invariants valued modulo n
   the atomic limit : 1 (-E2)_b, Z-valued (0, 0, 1), mod 2 (1, 0)
   a signed sum     : 1 (-E1)_a + 1 (-E2)_a - 1 (-E1)_b, Z-valued (0, 0, 1), mod 2 (0, 0)
   the Z-valued invariants agree and the Z2-valued ones differ: the invariants valued
   modulo n are not functions of the symmetry data vector, so a band set has them only
   through a set of orbitals known to carry it, the model's own or an atomic limit

3. splitting(r, bands=6): the six occupied bands against the two above them
   P4mm1' #99.164, double-valued: nsit, no realization of the valence bands and of the conduction bands adding up to the whole model's invariants valued modulo n   (.group, .nsit)
     Z-valued stable real-space invariants theta_1 to theta_3: the whole model (2, 2, 0) = valence (1, 1, 1) + conduction (1, 1, -1)   (.theta_Z, .valence.theta_Z, .conduction.theta_Z)
     invariants valued modulo n of the whole model: theta_4, theta_5 = (0, 1) mod 2   (.theta_Zn)
     atomic realizations of the valence bands, with (theta_4, theta_5) mod 2   (.valence.realizations)
       1 (-E2)_b + 1 (-E)_c   (1, 1)
       1 (-E1)_b + 2 (-E2)_b   (0, 0)
       1 (-E1)_a + 1 (-E2)_a + 1 (-E2)_b   (1, 0)
     atomic realizations of the conduction bands, with (theta_4, theta_5) mod 2   (.conduction.realizations)
       1 (-E1)_b   (0, 0)
     no pair of a valence and a conduction realization has invariants valued modulo n adding up to the whole model's   (.consistent_pairs)
   bands 4 and 5 are among the six: what their atomic limit in section 2 could not
   show, the Z2-valued invariants of the two sides of this gap do

4. splitting(r, bands=4): the same model, the gap two bands lower
   P4mm1' #99.164, double-valued: not nsit, 2 pairs of a valence and a conduction realization adding up to the whole model's invariants valued modulo n   (.group, .nsit, .consistent_pairs)
     Z-valued stable real-space invariants theta_1 to theta_3: the whole model (2, 2, 0) = valence (1, 1, 0) + conduction (1, 1, 0)   (.theta_Z, .valence.theta_Z, .conduction.theta_Z)
     invariants valued modulo n of the whole model: theta_4, theta_5 = (0, 1) mod 2   (.theta_Zn)
     atomic realizations of the valence bands, with (theta_4, theta_5) mod 2   (.valence.realizations)
       1 (-E)_c   (0, 1)
       1 (-E1)_b + 1 (-E2)_b   (1, 0)
       1 (-E1)_a + 1 (-E2)_a   (0, 0)
     atomic realizations of the conduction bands, with (theta_4, theta_5) mod 2   (.conduction.realizations)
       1 (-E)_c   (0, 1)
       1 (-E1)_b + 1 (-E2)_b   (1, 0)
       1 (-E1)_a + 1 (-E2)_a   (0, 0)
     pairs of a valence and a conduction realization whose invariants valued modulo n add up to the whole model's   (.consistent_pairs)
       1 (-E)_c with 1 (-E1)_a + 1 (-E2)_a
       1 (-E1)_a + 1 (-E2)_a with 1 (-E)_c
   the same Hamiltonian and the same eight bands, one gap lower: the criterion
   diagnoses the gap between bands 5 and 6, whose valence side holds bands 4 and 5,
   and not the gap between bands 3 and 4

5. the eight bands along GM-X-M-GM, with the two gaps marked
   bands 3 and 4    : gap 0.661624 over a 41x41 mesh
   bands 5 and 6    : gap 0.581572
   both gaps are open

